  "question": {
    "text": "A series <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></math> circuit is connected to a voltage source with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> . After a very large time, current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> behaves as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#8811;</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>:",
    "image": null
  },
